WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.723
Local AI performance depends on the machine, the model, and the configuration.

00:00:04.723 --> 00:00:09.347
Available RAM, accelerator memory where present, CPU speed, storage speed, model size,

00:00:09.347 --> 00:00:13.585
context length, and serving settings all influence response quality and latency.

00:00:13.585 --> 00:00:18.208
A workflow that feels smooth for one task may struggle with another.

00:00:18.208 --> 00:00:19.364
Reliability needs observation.

00:00:19.364 --> 00:00:23.602
Watch for memory pressure, slow responses, model loading time, failed requests,

00:00:23.602 --> 00:00:26.299
truncated context, repeated restarts, and user frustration.

00:00:26.299 --> 00:00:31.693
These signals show whether the workflow is still experimental or ready for heavier use.

00:00:31.693 --> 00:00:34.005
Important prompts, configuration notes, evaluation records,

00:00:34.005 --> 00:00:37.472
and workflow documentation should be backed up where appropriate.

00:00:37.472 --> 00:00:40.940
The goal is not to save every casual chat.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:46.334
The goal is to preserve the records needed to rebuild or understand important workflows.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:47.875
Updates should be tested.

00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:50.957
A new model file, changed configuration, updated client,

00:00:50.957 --> 00:00:55.195
or adjusted server setting can improve the workflow or break assumptions.

00:00:55.195 --> 00:00:59.048
Test important prompts and integrations before relying on the change.

00:00:59.048 --> 00:01:03.286
Sovereign AI can become important infrastructure for an individual or team.

00:01:03.286 --> 00:01:07.525
Dependable local AI needs basic care: ownership, notes, backups, version awareness,

00:01:07.525 --> 00:01:12.148
resource monitoring, safe shutdown, and a plan for troubleshooting when something changes.

00:01:12.148 --> 00:01:17.927
Operational discipline is what keeps a helpful local tool from becoming a fragile personal shortcut.

00:01:17.927 --> 00:01:21.780
If people rely on the workflow, it deserves routine maintenance.
